# Frontend Architecture

Strict layout for `apps/admin`, `apps/mobile`, and `apps/website`. Violations are review blockers.

## App layers

```text
src/
  app/                 # Framework routing only (Next App Router OR Vite router entry)
  modules/<domain>/    # Feature domains (auth, athlete, marketing, …)
    screens/           # Full pages / route bodies
    sections/          # Composable page sections
    lib/               # Domain data, hooks, API adapters for THIS domain
    components/        # Domain-private composites (optional)
  shared/              # Cross-domain app code (NOT packages/*)
    components/
    lib/
    hooks/
    providers/
  i18n/                # next-intl request config (Next apps)
```

## Hard rules

1. **Thin routes** — `app/**/page.tsx` (Next) or route elements (Vite) only wire metadata/params → module screens. No business UI in route files.
2. **Screens / sections** — PascalCase folder with exactly: `Name.tsx`, `Name.styles.ts`, `Name.types.ts`, `index.ts`. Styles via `tailwind-variants` (`tv`).
3. **No cross-module imports of internals** — import another module only via its public screen/section/`index` export, never deep `lib/` of a sibling domain.
4. **API only through `@repo/api`** — no raw `fetch` to Gym4Me backend from screens. Domain `lib/` may wrap `@repo/api` helpers.
5. **Auth** — authorization uses JWT `activeRole` only. Mobile uses account auth; admin uses admin auth. Session lives in `@repo/api` storage + app provider.
6. **Shared UI** — product composites go in `@repo/ui` (`cards` / `layout` / `kit` / `common`). App `shared/` is for app-shell glue only (providers, Capacitor, document meta).
7. **Icons** — `@repo/icons` only. **Primitives** — `@heroui/react` only.
8. **Mocks** — temporary fixtures live in `modules/<domain>/lib/*-data.ts` and must be replaceable by API adapters without touching screens' public props when possible.
9. **Aliases** — every app uses `@/*` → `src/*`.
10. **No demo / scaffold leftovers** in production routes. Dev galleries live under `/dev` (mobile) and are not the default `/`.
11. **Code splitting** — Admin screens load with `React.lazy`. Next apps keep routes thin and use `next/dynamic` for heavy client islands (maps, editors, GSAP, dnd-kit, health plugins). Do not eagerly import every screen from the router.
12. **Import cost** — Icons via `@repo/icons/Name`. UI via `@repo/ui/<category>/<Name>`. API factories via `@repo/api/<domain>`. Do not import `@repo/ui/kit` or `@repo/ui/cards` barrels from screens.
13. **Models** — Request/response shapes come from `@repo/api` DTOs. App `*.types.ts` files hold UI props only; do not duplicate API models.

## App responsibilities

| App | Role |
|-----|------|
| `mobile` | Multi-role product (athlete / coach / owner) + Capacitor |
| `admin` | Ops panel (Vite SPA) |
| `website` | Public / SEO marketing |

## Packages

| Package | Use for |
|---------|---------|
| `@repo/api` | HTTP client, domain APIs (`*.client` / `*.endpoint` / `*.dto` / `*.keys` / `*.hooks`), session storage |
| `@repo/ui` | Shared product UI (framework-agnostic; no hard `next` runtime deps) |
| `@repo/theme` / `@repo/icons` / `@repo/fonts` / `@repo/i18n` | Design system + copy |

## Website legacy

Marketing may temporarily keep `public/assets/{styles,scripts}` for GSAP/scroll contracts. Treat as **quarantined legacy** — do not add new BEM/CSS there; new UI is Tailwind + HeroUI + module sections.
